  "factor_name": "Volatility-persistence weighted medium-term residual reversal",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "-residual_return_40d * clip(volatility_80d / volatility_20d, 0.5, 3.0), lagged 1 session",
    "description": "For each tradable asset, subtract the cross-sectional mean 40-day return and reverse the residual. Multiply by the ratio of 80-day to 20-day daily log-return volatility, clipped to limit outliers. The one-session lag prevents look-ahead. Higher values indicate stronger contrarian preference, especially where short-term volatility is compressed relative to its longer baseline."
  },
